{"type":"message","id":"9317d816","parentId":"77de1b47","timestamp":"2026-01-31T22:01:38.177Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pivot the Polymarket bot at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/polymarket-copytrade/ from whale copytrading to a simple arbitrage detection system.\n\n## What exists:\n- Whale monitor (src/monitor.js) and paper trader (src/paper-trader.js) — keep these, but they become secondary\n- PM2 processes: polymarket-monitor, polymarket-paper\n- data/whales.json, data/whale-activity.jsonl, data/paper-portfolio.json\n\n## What to build:\n\n### 1. src/arbitrage-scanner.js (NEW — main process)\nConnect to Polymarket CLOB API via WebSocket (or polling if WS not available).\n- Polymarket CLOB API docs: https://docs.polymarket.com/\n- REST endpoint: GET https://clob.polymarket.com/markets for all active markets\n- Each market has tokens (YES/NO) with best bid/ask prices\n- For binary markets: check if best_ask_yes + best_ask_no < 1.00 (buy both sides cheap)\n- Also check if best_bid_yes + best_bid_no > 1.00 (sell both sides expensive — though this requires holding positions)\n- For multi-outcome markets (e.g. \"Who wins the election?\" with 5+ candidates): check if sum of all best_ask prices < 1.00\n\n### Detection logic:\n- Fetch all markets every 10 seconds (start with polling, upgrade to WS later)\n- For each binary market: compute spread = best_ask_yes + best_ask_no\n- If spread < 0.95: flag as arbitrage opportunity (5 cent buffer for fees + slippage)\n- Calculate available liquidity (min of ask sizes on both sides)\n- Calculate expected profit: (1.00 - spread) × min_liquidity\n- Log to data/arbitrage-opportunities.jsonl\n\n### 2. src/arbitrage-paper-trader.js (NEW)\n- When opportunity detected with profit > $0.50:\n  - Simulate buying both YES and NO at ask prices\n  - Track simulated P&L\n  - Log all paper trades to data/arbitrage-paper-trades.jsonl\n- Daily summary: total opportunities detected, paper trades taken, simulated P&L\n\n### 3. Telegram alerting\n- When opportunity with profit > $5 detected, send alert via writing to a file data/alerts-pending.jsonl\n- Format: { timestamp, market_slug, market_question, yes_ask, no_ask, spread, potential_profit, liquidity }\n\n### 4. Update ecosystem.config.cjs\n- Add polymarket-arbitrage process\n- Keep existing whale monitor processes\n\n### 5. Update STATE.md\n- Document the pivot from copytrading to arbitrage\n- Update architecture description\n\n## Technical notes:\n- Use node-fetch or built-in fetch for HTTP\n- Polymarket CLOB base URL: https://clob.polymarket.com\n- Key endpoints: /markets, /book (order book for specific token)\n- No API key needed for public read endpoints\n- Package.json already has dependencies installed\n\n## DO NOT:\n- Stop or remove the existing whale monitor\n- Use any real money or connect any wallet\n- Install heavy dependencies (no Gurobi, no IP solvers)\n\nStart the new arbitrage scanner via PM2 after building it. Test that it runs and finds data."}],"timestamp":1769896898176}}
