{"type":"message","id":"f34e0922","parentId":"35449c27","timestamp":"2026-01-31T22:09:04.527Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 processes running. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n## Completed\n\n**Built 2 new files:**\n- `src/arbitrage-scanner.js` — Polls Gamma API for 2000 active markets, fetches CLOB order books in batches of 20, checks for buy-both-sides and sell-both-sides arb on binary markets, and buy-all on multi-outcome markets. Logs to `data/arbitrage-opportunities.jsonl`, alerts to `data/alerts-pending.jsonl`.\n- `src/arbitrage-paper-trader.js` — Watches opportunities file, simulates trades on $0.50+ profit opps with 2% fee estimate, tracks P&L in `data/arbitrage-paper-state.json`.\n\n**Updated:**\n- `ecosystem.config.cjs` — Added `polymarket-arbitrage` and `polymarket-arb-paper` processes\n- `STATE.md` — Documented the pivot, new architecture, all key files\n\n**Running via PM2:**\n- `polymarket-arbitrage` ✅ online, scanning every 10s\n- `polymarket-arb-paper` ✅ online, monitoring for trades\n- Existing whale processes untouched ✅\n\n**Key finding:** After testing, Polymarket markets have spreads of 1.01-1.04 (ask_yes + ask_no), meaning markets are efficient with no arb below the 0.95 threshold. This is expected — the scanner will continue monitoring for when inefficiencies appear (e.g., during volatile news events)."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":368,"cacheRead":38367,"cacheWrite":437,"totalTokens":39173,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.0092,"cacheRead":0.0191835,"cacheWrite":0.00273125,"total":0.031119749999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1769897333261}}
